    rationale: "BELINDA randomised 322 patients to tisagenlecleucel or salvage chemotherapy with transplant in the second line and found median event-free survival of 3.0 months in both arms, while ZUMA-7 and TRANSFORM, testing the other two products in the same setting, were positive. The median time from leukapheresis to infusion in BELINDA was 52 days, and 25.9 per cent of the CAR-T group had progressed by week 6 against 13.8 per cent of the comparator group. TRANSCEND NHL 001 reported that 75 of 344 patients who underwent leukapheresis never received the product, which is attrition a response rate does not show.",
