    rationale: "Rituximab was approved in 1997 and biosimilars have been available for years, yet supply remains intermittent in much of Africa, south Asia and Latin America. Asparaginase is the drug that makes extranodal NK/T-cell lymphoma treatable, and it is subject to recurrent global shortages. Burkitt lymphoma, which is curable with chemotherapy alone in a high proportion of children, is concentrated in the equatorial African belt where Burkitt first described it. The arithmetic favours supply over discovery.",
